      "id": "r:3744459738",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "In-memory index state advances ahead of persisted data during batching; an interrupt causes Commit() to write advanced state with a stale locator, corrupting the index on restart",
      "quote": "The most serious issue seems to me that `Commit()` during interrupt writes advanced `m_muhash` alongside a stale locator, which causes `CoinStatsIndex::CustomInit` to reject the index as corrupted on restart.",
      "blocking": true,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:5388740037"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:2906884044",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "BlockFilterIndex writes flat files to disk eagerly per block, which is misaligned with LevelDB batching and risks orphaned flat file data on interrupt",
      "quote": "We seem to be writing to disk to eagerly here, this also is misaligned with the batching.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
